      "year": 2013,
      "kind": "milestone",
      "title": "Started at Stuyvesant",
      "detail": "September 2013. There was a NASCAR driver in my graduating class who had been training since he was a kid.",
      "learning": {
        "kind": "advice",
        "at": "2026",
        "text": "Being surrounded by people who are genuinely exceptional at one thing is humbling, and the wrong lesson to take from it is to go find your one thing and grind. The right one — the one it took me years to act on — is that you need to be good at more than one thing to excel. The overlap is where you're actually rare."
      },
      "place": {
